@startuml
title POST /api/ai-agents-teams/runs/{run_id}/output/prepare + /send — owner-only output reveal
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Run owner" as Owner #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.revealOutput(runId)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nchain + observer" as Chain #FFE4A6
participant "Continuation store\n(encrypted artifacts)" as Store #E8DDF5

Owner -> SDK : revealOutput(runId)

group Phase 1 — prepare (no body; deploys nothing)
SDK -> API : POST .../runs/{run_id}/output/prepare
API -> Domain : prepare reveal
Domain -> Chain : getRun(run_id) — owner-scrubbed record
alt no run record
Domain --> API : 404 — run capability not found
else no output hashes on the record
Domain --> API : 409 — run has no recorded output\n(running, suspended, resuming, or legacy)
else terminal run with committed output hashes
Domain -> Store : locate the Output artifact and verify\nits hashes against the on-chain record
Domain -> Domain : mint reveal_id (UUIDv7); render the\nclaimOutputReveal contract
Domain --> API : RevealOutputResp { reveal_id, contract,\n  issued_at, output hashes }
API --> SDK : PrepareResponse { response, token }\n(the token binds the path run id)
end
end

group Sign and send
SDK -> SDK : sign the contract locally (secp256k1);\nthe wallet key never leaves the client
SDK -> API : POST .../runs/{run_id}/output/send\n{ prepare_request: run_id, prepare echo,\n  signed contract, token }
API -> Domain : deploy signed reveal
Domain -> Chain : deploy claimOutputReveal(run_id, reveal_id)
note right of Chain #FFF6C9
The clause is the verifier of record: the ledger
scrubs owner from every read, so only the chain
can adjudicate this claim. On success it appends
an actor-less outputRevealed event and
acknowledges { revealId, output hashes } over
the deploy-id channel.
end note
alt claim aborts on chain
Chain --> Domain : deploy errored
Domain -> Chain : re-read the run to name the cause
Domain --> API : 403 unauthorized signer\n(404 / 409 if the record itself explains it)
API --> SDK : refusal — nothing was disclosed
else claim lands
Chain --> Domain : positive acknowledgment read back\n(no acknowledgment — pre-clause chain — fails closed)
Domain -> Domain : verify ack reveal_id and hashes against\nthe prepare echo
Domain -> Store : locate + decrypt the Output artifact\nchecked against the acknowledged hashes
Domain --> API : the run's final output value
API --> SDK : 200 — output JSON over the\nsigner's channel only
SDK --> Owner : full response value
end
end

note over API #FFF0C7
The public run ledger records that a reveal happened
(outputRevealed) — never the value, and never who
revealed: publishing the actor would de-anonymize the
owner the ledger deliberately scrubs.
end note
@enduml
